[{"content":"A securitisation holds a collateral pool with par balance $76,600,000. It has issued a senior tranche A of $60,600,000 paying 4% interest per period on its outstanding balance, and a junior tranche B of $4,900,000 paying 8% interest per period (B's principal is not repaid during the two periods). Equity receives whatever is left. In each of two periods, the pool collects interest of 9% of its par balance at the start of the period plus scheduled principal of $1,000,000. At the end of each period, par falls by the scheduled principal and by that period's defaults (period 1: $6,500,000; period 2: $1,300,000), with no recoveries. Each period's collections are paid in this order: (1) senior interest on tranche A's balance at the start of the period; (2) the overcollateralisation (OC) test: if end-of-period par divided by tranche A's balance is below 125%, cash is diverted to repay tranche A principal, exactly the amount that brings the ratio back to 125% (or all remaining cash if that is less); (3) junior interest on tranche B, where any shortfall is lost, not carried forward; (4) everything left goes to equity. Tranche A's balance falls only through OC diversions. First: what is the OC ratio at the end of period 1, before any diversion (end-of-period par as a percentage of tranche A's balance)? Give the percentage rounded to 2 decimal places, without the % sign. Reply with only the number.","role":"user"},{"content":"114.03","role":"assistant"},{"content":"How much cash is diverted to repay tranche A principal in period 1? Give the amount in whole dollars. Reply with only the number.","role":"user"},{"content":"5320000","role":"assistant"},{"content":"How much cash does junior tranche B receive in period 2? Give the amount in whole dollars. Reply with only the number.","role":"user"},{"content":"392000","role":"assistant"},{"content":"What is the total cash received by equity over both periods? Give the amount in whole dollars. Reply with only the number."